WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.123 --> 00:00:00.956
More flour!?

00:00:00.956 --> 00:00:01.959
I'm going rogue.

00:00:01.959 --> 00:00:03.352
It smells like pizza.

00:00:03.352 --> 00:00:05.145
Is it poison if I just eat like this?

00:00:05.145 --> 00:00:06.417
When do you put the yeast in, I wonder?

00:00:06.417 --> 00:00:08.453
- [Male, Offcamera] Way long ago.

00:00:08.453 --> 00:00:10.126
(ding)

00:00:10.126 --> 00:00:13.209
(fun carnival music)

00:00:18.999 --> 00:00:20.845
Today, we're in the Tasty Kitchen,

00:00:20.845 --> 00:00:22.844
where the Try Guys will try their hand

00:00:22.844 --> 00:00:24.177
at making bread.

00:00:25.011 --> 00:00:26.163
But, there's a catch.

00:00:26.163 --> 00:00:27.920
They will not be getting a recipe,

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.277
or any instructions how to do it.

00:00:30.277 --> 00:00:31.357
They will just have to go by

00:00:31.357 --> 00:00:32.626
their own initiative and

00:00:32.626 --> 00:00:34.271
the ingredients they have chosen.

00:00:34.271 --> 00:00:35.902
Oh no, I ... Oh no.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:38.187
- [Joan] The bakers will
be judged by our panel.

00:00:38.187 --> 00:00:41.907
Alexis deBoschnek from
Buzzfeed's own Tasty Kitchen.

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:43.674
Hannah Hart, from her show,

00:00:43.674 --> 00:00:46.266
I Hart Food on the Food Network.

00:00:46.266 --> 00:00:48.210
And Zack Hall, from LA's famous

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.990
Clark Street Bakery.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.050
Bread is very simple on paper.

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.122
You get the flour,

00:00:53.122 --> 00:00:54.356
and by adding water to it

00:00:54.356 --> 00:00:55.508
it makes gluten.

00:00:55.508 --> 00:00:57.217
Which is able to trap gas.

00:00:57.217 --> 00:00:59.303
We use the salt just to give bread flavor.

00:00:59.303 --> 00:01:00.502
Without it, it would be bland.

00:01:00.502 --> 00:01:03.762
And we use the yeast to
make the gas in bread.

00:01:03.762 --> 00:01:05.963
That's why bread is inflated,

00:01:05.963 --> 00:01:07.377
and it is nice and fluffy.

00:01:07.377 --> 00:01:09.574
This is an extremely
easy thing to mess up.

00:01:09.574 --> 00:01:11.598
Especially if you don't have

00:01:11.598 --> 00:01:13.592
a lot of practice doing it.

00:01:13.592 --> 00:01:14.549
Bread.

00:01:14.549 --> 00:01:15.636
Bread is one of those things

00:01:15.636 --> 00:01:17.544
that everybody has eaten.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:18.767
But how do you make bread?

00:01:18.767 --> 00:01:19.962
I don't bake.

00:01:19.962 --> 00:01:22.158
I don't cook anything.

00:01:22.158 --> 00:01:22.991
I used to be a chemist,

00:01:22.991 --> 00:01:25.723
so I know that baking is
a very precise science.

00:01:25.723 --> 00:01:27.738
And like math, I can look at a problem

00:01:27.738 --> 00:01:29.422
and know it's algebra.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.708
But I'm not going to know

00:01:30.708 --> 00:01:32.000
what the answer is.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.311
We're just going to
fucking wing it, you guys.

00:01:34.311 --> 00:01:35.410
I think I'm going to win this today.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:36.243
I think, for once,

00:01:36.243 --> 00:01:37.887
Keith is like the leader

00:01:37.887 --> 00:01:40.532
because I think I know what I'm doing.

00:01:40.532 --> 00:01:41.494
Ready, guys?

00:01:41.494 --> 00:01:42.327
On your mark.

00:01:42.327 --> 00:01:43.402
Get set.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:45.474
And try and bake!

00:01:45.474 --> 00:01:47.489
To get started, our bakers must first

00:01:47.489 --> 00:01:49.974
select their ingredients
from the Tasty Pantry.

00:01:49.974 --> 00:01:52.035
And I hope they choose wisely.

00:01:52.035 --> 00:01:53.628
Oh, liquid bread.

00:01:53.628 --> 00:01:54.709
(bottlecap pops off)

00:01:54.709 --> 00:01:56.158
Oh, boy, this is overwhelming.

00:01:56.158 --> 00:01:57.310
There's a lot of stuff.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:58.866
I would suggest to start with a loaf

00:01:58.866 --> 00:02:00.613
of just flour, water, salt, and yeast.

00:02:00.613 --> 00:02:01.918
You know, it's sort of like the benchmark.

00:02:01.918 --> 00:02:03.080
It's like, do this before you move

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.610
onto adding other ingredients to it.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:06.850
Do you guys know where gluten is?

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:07.758
I think I just need salt,

00:02:07.758 --> 00:02:08.841
yeast, flour.

00:02:09.939 --> 00:02:11.811
Is there anything else I should get?

00:02:11.811 --> 00:02:12.963
Sugar?

00:02:12.963 --> 00:02:13.915
I got honey.

00:02:13.915 --> 00:02:15.382
Today I'm going to make a white bread.

00:02:15.382 --> 00:02:16.570
White bread's a lot like me.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.416
Plain, not super healthy,

00:02:18.416 --> 00:02:20.143
and generally likable.

00:02:20.143 --> 00:02:21.486
Thyme.

00:02:21.486 --> 00:02:22.509
Cayenne.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:24.454
I love black roasted sesame seeds.

00:02:24.454 --> 00:02:25.287
I love alcohol.

00:02:25.287 --> 00:02:26.190
I love spice.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.433
Those two things represent me.

00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:28.266
I'm going to try to find a way

00:02:28.266 --> 00:02:29.766
to fold it into bread.

00:02:29.766 --> 00:02:31.359
I don't know if either belong there,

00:02:31.359 --> 00:02:33.094
but I'm going to make it happen.

00:02:33.094 --> 00:02:34.194
My ancestors made the mistake

00:02:34.194 --> 00:02:35.427
of forgetting yeast in their bread.

00:02:35.427 --> 00:02:37.542
I am not going to follow
in their footsteps.

00:02:37.542 --> 00:02:38.375
Boom.

00:02:38.375 --> 00:02:39.342
Three things of yeast.

00:02:39.342 --> 00:02:41.161
My approach is just going to be...

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.106
I'm just going to grab

00:02:42.106 --> 00:02:43.671
as much bullshit as possible,

00:02:43.671 --> 00:02:45.138
and hope that something happens.

00:02:45.138 --> 00:02:47.090
I don't want to create poison.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.180
(offscreen laughter)

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:49.093
How many eggs do I need?

00:02:49.093 --> 00:02:50.537
Fuck it, I'll take all of them.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:51.787
Oooh, cinnamon!

00:02:52.635 --> 00:02:53.885
Oh my god, yes.

00:02:54.966 --> 00:02:56.182
In my family, me and my dad were

00:02:56.182 --> 00:02:58.422
the only two people that
liked cinnamon raisin bread.

00:02:58.422 --> 00:02:59.835
So it's a very special memory for me,

00:02:59.835 --> 00:03:01.762
and I'm going to try and recreate

00:03:01.762 --> 00:03:03.553
the cinnamon raisin bread

00:03:03.553 --> 00:03:05.810
that we bought at the store.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:06.643
- [Joan] Ready!

00:03:06.643 --> 00:03:07.476
Set!

00:03:07.476 --> 00:03:08.806
Bake!

00:03:08.806 --> 00:03:09.639
Okay.

00:03:09.639 --> 00:03:10.860
What are we grabbing? What?

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:11.931
I need a bowl, I need a bowl.

00:03:11.931 --> 00:03:12.764
Need a big bowl.

00:03:12.764 --> 00:03:14.262
Need a small bowl.

00:03:14.262 --> 00:03:15.289
So the first thing you want to do

00:03:15.289 --> 00:03:16.962
when you're making bread is to

00:03:16.962 --> 00:03:18.203
mix together your ingredients.

00:03:18.203 --> 00:03:20.309
First ingredient of bread: bread crumbs.

00:03:20.309 --> 00:03:21.883
Thyme to bake.

00:03:21.883 --> 00:03:22.716
Nobody?

00:03:22.716 --> 00:03:23.791
I have this sugar from Japan.

00:03:23.791 --> 00:03:25.142
I didn't grab sugar.

00:03:25.142 --> 00:03:26.340
I grabbed honey.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.265
Which is essentially sugar

00:03:28.265 --> 00:03:30.397
that's been vomited out of a bee's mouth.

00:03:30.397 --> 00:03:31.610
My bread is going to be a

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.854
honey white bread, and I'm going to

00:03:33.854 --> 00:03:35.526
give it an egg wash on top,

00:03:35.526 --> 00:03:37.498
so it looks extra special.

00:03:37.498 --> 00:03:38.371
Cayenne!

00:03:38.371 --> 00:03:39.559
(sneezes)

00:03:39.559 --> 00:03:40.901
Are you starting with
spices? Is that ... ?

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.468
I'm just mixing them together.

00:03:42.468 --> 00:03:45.444
(loud bangs)

00:03:45.444 --> 00:03:46.769
My bread is going to be the

00:03:46.769 --> 00:03:48.442
drunken 12 spice loaf.

00:03:48.442 --> 00:03:50.810
It has an entire pack of IPA beer,

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:52.741
and lots of spice.

00:03:52.741 --> 00:03:54.056
So, what's your game plan, Ned?

00:03:54.056 --> 00:03:55.326
First, I'm going to make a

00:03:55.326 --> 00:03:56.989
cinnamon and sugar mixture,

00:03:56.989 --> 00:03:58.406
and set it aside.

00:03:59.383 --> 00:04:00.872
It's going to give it some color,

00:04:00.872 --> 00:04:03.896
some swirls, and some sweetness.

00:04:03.896 --> 00:04:06.805
Today, I'm making a cinnamon raisin bread.

00:04:06.805 --> 00:04:09.884
It reminds me of growing up eating toast.

00:04:09.884 --> 00:04:13.134
I got three different types of flour.

00:04:14.204 --> 00:04:15.262
I'm just going to go with this one,

00:04:15.262 --> 00:04:16.371
because it sounds the fanciest.

00:04:16.371 --> 00:04:17.737
Buckwheat flour.

00:04:17.737 --> 00:04:19.774
Getting buckwheat on.

00:04:19.774 --> 00:04:21.853
Today, I am baking a buckwheat loaf,

00:04:21.853 --> 00:04:23.741
including some of my favorite things.

00:04:23.741 --> 00:04:26.901
Like Nutella, gummy
bears, and bread crumbs.

00:04:26.901 --> 00:04:29.324
I am starting with yeast.

00:04:29.324 --> 00:04:30.737
So what is yeast?

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:33.068
Is this the stuff that
gives women infections?

00:04:33.068 --> 00:04:34.237
Is this different yeast?

00:04:34.237 --> 00:04:36.773
So one of these yeast packets is 14 grams.

00:04:36.773 --> 00:04:37.971
Just a little bit of that.

00:04:37.971 --> 00:04:39.184
There we go.

00:04:39.184 --> 00:04:40.635
That's all the yeast you need.

00:04:40.635 --> 00:04:41.914
Yeast is going in, baby.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:42.958
Let's see what happens.

00:04:42.958 --> 00:04:45.601
As everyone knows, all chemical reactions

00:04:45.601 --> 00:04:47.890
get accelerated by agitation,

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.389
so I'm going to stir my yeast.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:53.009
You know yeast is in beer, don't you?

00:04:53.009 --> 00:04:55.384
If Eugene's bringing more
yeast, then I want more yeast.

00:04:55.384 --> 00:04:57.681
I'm supposed to put some
amount of this water

00:04:57.681 --> 00:05:00.261
into this bowl, and then
add some amount of sugar

00:05:00.261 --> 00:05:03.213
in as well, because the
sugar activates the yeast.

00:05:03.213 --> 00:05:04.663
You don't need to activate the yeast.

00:05:04.663 --> 00:05:06.564
If it's dried like this,
you can just add it in

00:05:06.564 --> 00:05:08.381
straight with the dry ingredients.

00:05:08.381 --> 00:05:10.874
Mix it, add the water,
it'll do it's thing.

00:05:10.874 --> 00:05:11.820
We'll put in the flour.

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:12.653
Pour it all.

00:05:12.653 --> 00:05:13.486
Get it.

00:05:13.486 --> 00:05:14.319
Get in there.

00:05:14.319 --> 00:05:15.152
Buck buck buck.

00:05:15.152 --> 00:05:16.555
All about the ratio.

00:05:16.555 --> 00:05:19.259
Next we'll go with 20 grams of salt.

00:05:19.259 --> 00:05:20.433
Mazel tov!

00:05:20.433 --> 00:05:21.811
This is what they do in the cooking shows,

00:05:21.811 --> 00:05:23.241
so let's do it like that.

00:05:23.241 --> 00:05:25.529
So I'm just going to put in a tablespoon.

00:05:25.529 --> 00:05:26.444
Now we can add our water.

00:05:26.444 --> 00:05:27.878
Make a nice soft dough.

00:05:27.878 --> 00:05:31.114
- [Keith] You should use water.

00:05:31.114 --> 00:05:32.120
Here, now, you just want to mix it

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.831
until all of the water has been absorbed

00:05:34.831 --> 00:05:36.242
and it's homogenized, so there's

00:05:36.242 --> 00:05:38.421
no pieces of dry flour remaining,

00:05:38.421 --> 00:05:40.581
and there's no clumps.

00:05:40.581 --> 00:05:42.319
You look like you're
doing very well, actually.

00:05:42.319 --> 00:05:44.352
I have watched a lot of cooking shows.

00:05:44.352 --> 00:05:46.370
They roll the dough into a little ball.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:47.870
Does egg go in bread?

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.548
Because I'm putting it in there.

00:05:49.548 --> 00:05:51.149
Why does mine look like doodoo?

00:05:51.149 --> 00:05:52.434
Did I fuck up something?

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:53.875
You need to get some more flour in there,

00:05:53.875 --> 00:05:55.603
because that's more like, um.

00:05:55.603 --> 00:05:57.468
Mud pies, than anything else.

00:05:57.468 --> 00:05:58.301
Any real flour?

00:05:58.301 --> 00:05:59.690
I don't want to open a new flour.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:01.382
Eugene, I'm going to
borrow some flour, buddy.

00:06:01.382 --> 00:06:02.472
There's one thing this dough needs,

00:06:02.472 --> 00:06:04.378
and it's a little more love.

00:06:04.378 --> 00:06:06.060
You want to make sure you
knead your bread enough.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.851
The way to tell whether
you knead it enough

00:06:07.851 --> 00:06:09.642
is it will change from some sort of putty

00:06:09.642 --> 00:06:12.192
into kind of holding it's
own shape a little more.

00:06:12.192 --> 00:06:13.514
It'll look smooth, it'll look shiny.

00:06:13.514 --> 00:06:14.369
This feels a lot like I'm

00:06:14.369 --> 00:06:16.959
massaging a really squishy butt.

00:06:16.959 --> 00:06:19.218
It's taking me forever
to fucking knead this.

00:06:19.218 --> 00:06:20.750
And I need this!

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.559
Y'all, this is coming together!

00:06:22.559 --> 00:06:24.612
- [Keith] How is yours that color?

00:06:24.612 --> 00:06:26.520
I don't know, I tried to be fancy.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:27.773
Why is-- Why?

00:06:27.773 --> 00:06:30.444
From that point on, you
want to be hands off.

00:06:30.444 --> 00:06:32.011
You don't want to be too rough with it.

00:06:32.011 --> 00:06:33.918
I knead this, baby!

00:06:33.918 --> 00:06:35.179
Because everything you do to it

00:06:35.179 --> 00:06:36.835
will knock gas out of it,

00:06:36.835 --> 00:06:39.984
and make it denser and
harder to bake through.

00:06:39.984 --> 00:06:41.515
Beer volcano!

00:06:41.515 --> 00:06:44.369
Look, the more solid stuff I put in here,

00:06:44.369 --> 00:06:45.897
the better shot I got.

00:06:45.897 --> 00:06:48.041
I did find a beer bottle cap in it before,

00:06:48.041 --> 00:06:49.029
but I took it out.

00:06:49.029 --> 00:06:50.504
At this point, you're just shaping it

00:06:50.504 --> 00:06:51.899
so it looks like a loaf of bread.

00:06:51.899 --> 00:06:52.732
You want to make sure

00:06:52.732 --> 00:06:53.647
there's not too much flour.

00:06:53.647 --> 00:06:54.483
Just enough.

00:06:54.483 --> 00:06:55.347
Otherwise it prevents the dough

00:06:55.347 --> 00:06:56.536
from sticking to itself.

00:06:56.536 --> 00:06:59.388
I've got my bread all rolled up,

00:06:59.388 --> 00:07:02.503
with cinnamon and sugar and raisins.

00:07:02.503 --> 00:07:03.715
Right now, you know what it looks like?

00:07:03.715 --> 00:07:05.660
It looks like one of
those airplane pillows.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:06.849
This is my lump.

00:07:06.849 --> 00:07:08.397
It's a little bit of buckwheat.

00:07:08.397 --> 00:07:09.569
Some Nutella in there,

00:07:09.569 --> 00:07:11.539
because everyone loves Nutella.

00:07:11.539 --> 00:07:12.708
Threw in some Fruity Pebs,

00:07:12.708 --> 00:07:14.311
for the nostalgia factor.

00:07:14.311 --> 00:07:15.391
Here is my bread.

00:07:15.391 --> 00:07:16.224
Nice and ready.

00:07:16.224 --> 00:07:17.649
I hate that Eugene's dough

00:07:17.649 --> 00:07:19.881
looks pretty okay right now.

00:07:19.881 --> 00:07:21.931
After you've shaped it, then it proofs.

00:07:21.931 --> 00:07:24.443
What I like to do at this point is to

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:25.892
stick it in the fridge overnight.

00:07:25.892 --> 00:07:28.233
It'll rise really slow
at a cool temperature.

00:07:28.233 --> 00:07:29.801
The next morning when you come back to it,

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:31.601
you'll see it's doubled in volume,

00:07:31.601 --> 00:07:33.228
and it's ready to be baked.

00:07:33.228 --> 00:07:35.379
- [Joan] So it's been
quite a day for our bakers.

00:07:35.379 --> 00:07:37.577
And now they're ready
to put their dough aside

00:07:37.577 --> 00:07:39.197
to proof overnight.

00:07:39.197 --> 00:07:41.789
Oh, I hope they don't fuck it up.

00:07:41.789 --> 00:07:44.956
(happy idyllic music)

00:07:51.021 --> 00:07:53.217
(sheep baas)

00:07:53.217 --> 00:07:56.349
It's day two of this
exciting baking challenge.

00:07:56.349 --> 00:07:57.825
Everyone's waiting to see.

00:07:57.825 --> 00:07:59.825
Have their breads risen?

00:08:00.799 --> 00:08:02.145
- [ Ned] My yeast was
foaming, so hopefully

00:08:02.145 --> 00:08:04.422
things work out okay.

00:08:04.422 --> 00:08:07.554
I'm just worried it's going
to be too big, really.

00:08:07.554 --> 00:08:08.608
- [Zach] I think no matter what happens,

00:08:08.608 --> 00:08:09.894
we're all impressed, you know?

00:08:09.894 --> 00:08:10.727
It's all about the journey,

00:08:10.727 --> 00:08:11.560
not the destination.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:12.845
- [ Keith] It was already
rising pretty well,

00:08:12.845 --> 00:08:13.961
by the end of yesterday,

00:08:13.961 --> 00:08:16.121
so I have good hopes for it.

00:08:16.121 --> 00:08:18.299
- [Eugene] I think I did
pretty poorly yesterday.

00:08:18.299 --> 00:08:20.209
Might have been one of
my worst performances

00:08:20.209 --> 00:08:21.774
in Try Guys history.

00:08:21.774 --> 00:08:23.249
Let's see.

00:08:23.249 --> 00:08:25.684
Okay, let's see it.

00:08:25.684 --> 00:08:26.528
Whoa.

00:08:26.528 --> 00:08:27.609
Oh no!

00:08:27.609 --> 00:08:29.000
No, it's good.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:31.649
I didn't expect it to become flat.

00:08:31.649 --> 00:08:32.739
Like a soup.

00:08:32.739 --> 00:08:34.287
Oh my god!

00:08:34.287 --> 00:08:35.746
It went from an airline pillow

00:08:35.746 --> 00:08:37.582
to a buttpad.

00:08:37.582 --> 00:08:38.415
Hey!

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:41.425
It rose a little bit!

00:08:41.425 --> 00:08:44.386
It looks like a stale turd.

00:08:44.386 --> 00:08:45.386
Holy shit!

00:08:46.906 --> 00:08:48.068
Still smells like beer.

00:08:48.068 --> 00:08:48.901
This looks crazy.

00:08:48.901 --> 00:08:50.146
This is awful, and it's a monster,

00:08:50.146 --> 00:08:51.605
and hopefully I can bake it.

00:08:51.605 --> 00:08:52.640
Woo!

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:55.124
Okay, so let's talk about how to bake it.

00:08:55.124 --> 00:08:56.859
So I'm going to try and make a

00:08:56.859 --> 00:08:59.026
cinnamon bundt cake bread.

00:09:00.658 --> 00:09:02.828
Cake is really just a type of bread.

00:09:02.828 --> 00:09:03.661
One of the most beautiful things

00:09:03.661 --> 00:09:05.964
you can do with bread is a signature.

00:09:05.964 --> 00:09:07.298
Something that lets everybody know

00:09:07.298 --> 00:09:08.378
that it's your bread,

00:09:08.378 --> 00:09:09.674
and not anyone else's bread.

00:09:09.674 --> 00:09:11.105
So I'm going to split it

00:09:11.105 --> 00:09:12.689
with a K, for Keith.

00:09:12.689 --> 00:09:14.597
How does he know so much about bread?

00:09:14.597 --> 00:09:15.768
I'm just going to throw butter on it.

00:09:15.768 --> 00:09:18.000
Yeah, now we got a real buttery dough.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.014
Oh!

00:09:19.014 --> 00:09:20.501
Oh, it's squirting.

00:09:20.501 --> 00:09:22.795
To complete my bread,

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:24.549
I'm going to give it a nice crust

00:09:24.549 --> 00:09:26.189
of pretzels and chocolate.

00:09:26.189 --> 00:09:27.578
(bangs)

00:09:27.578 --> 00:09:28.467
Oh, it did nothing.

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:30.967
(metal bangs)

00:09:32.078 --> 00:09:33.331
(laughs)

00:09:33.331 --> 00:09:34.322
(bangs)

00:09:34.322 --> 00:09:36.109
I can't even break a pretzel right?

00:09:36.109 --> 00:09:37.117
I'm going to make a braid.

00:09:37.117 --> 00:09:37.950
If there's one thing I know how to do

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.267
with two sisters is braid.

00:09:39.267 --> 00:09:40.157
I really respect what's happening

00:09:40.157 --> 00:09:41.401
on this side of the room.

00:09:41.401 --> 00:09:43.020
We're getting a little
avant garde with it.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.287
We're mixing it up.

00:09:45.287 --> 00:09:46.352
(gasps)

00:09:46.352 --> 00:09:47.685
Yes, queen, yes.

00:09:49.565 --> 00:09:52.013
You bake for 40 minutes
about about 475 degrees.

00:09:52.013 --> 00:09:53.292
I'm doing 350 degrees.

00:09:53.292 --> 00:09:54.125
40 minutes?

00:09:54.125 --> 00:09:54.958
I don't know.

00:09:54.958 --> 00:09:56.990
I'm just going to say 30 minutes.

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:58.276
The thing is, I wanted to preheat

00:09:58.276 --> 00:09:59.305
mine at 375 as well.

00:09:59.305 --> 00:10:00.138
Wow.

00:10:00.138 --> 00:10:01.580
Because of frozen foods.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:02.818
I would say that if I'm doing it,

00:10:02.818 --> 00:10:04.335
that's maybe a sign you shouldn't do it.

00:10:04.335 --> 00:10:05.936
I'm going to do a little egg wash on it,

00:10:05.936 --> 00:10:07.709
so that it even looks sexier.

00:10:07.709 --> 00:10:09.518
Ooh, that's not washing
the way I want it to.

00:10:09.518 --> 00:10:10.805
Did you add some water in there too,

00:10:10.805 --> 00:10:12.018
or just egg?

00:10:12.018 --> 00:10:12.949
No, just egg.

00:10:12.949 --> 00:10:14.009
Should it be water too?

00:10:14.009 --> 00:10:14.842
A little bit.

00:10:14.842 --> 00:10:15.675
Welp.

00:10:15.675 --> 00:10:16.508
I see that there's some

00:10:16.508 --> 00:10:17.716
bubbling happening down there.

00:10:17.716 --> 00:10:18.549
Smells good.

00:10:18.549 --> 00:10:19.395
Why is it bubbling?

00:10:19.395 --> 00:10:21.056
That's a cake pan, for starters.

00:10:21.056 --> 00:10:23.271
Well, I gotta stand out
in this competition.

00:10:23.271 --> 00:10:25.646
Oh, I think you will. (laughs)

00:10:25.646 --> 00:10:27.660
It looks like a cottage loaf.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:28.869
Oh, okay.

00:10:28.869 --> 00:10:29.702
That sounds fancy.

00:10:29.702 --> 00:10:30.535
I'll take that.

00:10:30.535 --> 00:10:31.450
I think I'm good.

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:32.414
I think I'm going to take it out.

00:10:32.414 --> 00:10:33.737
Alright, there you go.

00:10:33.737 --> 00:10:35.276
Then, what you're left with is

00:10:35.276 --> 00:10:36.374
something like this.

00:10:36.374 --> 00:10:37.293
A loaf of bread that's got

00:10:37.293 --> 00:10:38.462
a nice color to it,

00:10:38.462 --> 00:10:39.533
nice and even shape,

00:10:39.533 --> 00:10:40.657
nice volume.

00:10:40.657 --> 00:10:42.189
This is really amazing.

00:10:42.189 --> 00:10:43.022
I can't believe it,

00:10:43.022 --> 00:10:44.105
I'm going to fucking win.

00:10:44.105 --> 00:10:45.374
That's bread!

00:10:45.374 --> 00:10:46.869
The egg wash definitely remained

00:10:46.869 --> 00:10:48.470
just egg on top of bread.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:50.433
It certainly smells like eggs, but

00:10:50.433 --> 00:10:52.485
otherwise I think it's good.

00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:53.834
I assume you put butter on everything

00:10:53.834 --> 00:10:56.167
because butter is delicious.

00:10:58.697 --> 00:10:59.530
Aaah!

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:01.315
It's bread!

00:11:01.315 --> 00:11:03.309
(blows air)

00:11:03.309 --> 00:11:05.309
- [Eugene] Sesame seeds.

00:11:08.314 --> 00:11:10.205
Welcome to the final judging.

00:11:10.205 --> 00:11:11.537
Where we will find out

00:11:11.537 --> 00:11:13.435
who is the top baker.

00:11:13.435 --> 00:11:15.739
We'll be judging on three categories:

00:11:15.739 --> 00:11:16.845
Presentation.

00:11:16.845 --> 00:11:18.161
Taste.

00:11:18.161 --> 00:11:20.193
And, is it bread?

00:11:20.193 --> 00:11:22.732
Ned, will you please present your bread?

00:11:22.732 --> 00:11:25.531
Judges, I present to you

00:11:25.531 --> 00:11:27.637
Ned's Cinnamon Raisin.

00:11:27.637 --> 00:11:28.728
Is that a bundt cake?

00:11:28.728 --> 00:11:29.561
It is.

00:11:29.561 --> 00:11:32.805
A bundt pan was used
to make the bread, yes.

00:11:32.805 --> 00:11:34.046
The 'bread.'

00:11:34.046 --> 00:11:35.551
It smells pretty sweet.

00:11:35.551 --> 00:11:37.305
And it's got a nice heft to it.

00:11:37.305 --> 00:11:38.215
- [Ned] Thank you, chef.

00:11:38.215 --> 00:11:39.312
Yeah, let's cut into this.

00:11:39.312 --> 00:11:40.814
(all gasp)

00:11:40.814 --> 00:11:42.814
Well, you got the swirl.

00:11:43.895 --> 00:11:44.787
- [Ned] Wow!

00:11:44.787 --> 00:11:45.913
The inside is gorgeous.

00:11:45.913 --> 00:11:46.746
Yes.
Yeah.

00:11:46.746 --> 00:11:49.872
Let's see how it taste, maybe.

00:11:49.872 --> 00:11:50.705
Oh, man.

00:11:53.472 --> 00:11:54.305
I think that about sums up

00:11:54.305 --> 00:11:56.472
what I think of the taste.

00:11:57.359 --> 00:11:59.287
Where is the bitterness coming from?

00:11:59.287 --> 00:12:00.454
Give it a try.

00:12:01.519 --> 00:12:03.156
Need some milk right about now, right?

00:12:03.156 --> 00:12:05.180
I think it's a good first try for sure,

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:07.170
but definitely could use a little bit

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:08.350
more sugar and salt next time.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:09.358
Just to get the flavor.

00:12:09.358 --> 00:12:10.706
It's a little bit bland.

00:12:10.706 --> 00:12:12.643
So judges, my question now is,

00:12:12.643 --> 00:12:13.643
is it bread?

00:12:14.515 --> 00:12:15.907
It is bread-like.

00:12:15.907 --> 00:12:18.250
But there's so much more it wants to be.

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.570
The more I eat it, the more I'm into it.

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.235
That is called Stockholm Syndrome.

00:12:22.235 --> 00:12:25.331
(all laugh)

00:12:25.331 --> 00:12:26.258
- [Hannah] Ooooh.

00:12:26.258 --> 00:12:27.770
- [Keith] Here it comes.

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:29.277
Oh, is that an egg wash?

00:12:29.277 --> 00:12:30.758
Just initially, the first scent

00:12:30.758 --> 00:12:32.947
I'm getting off of it is the yolk.

00:12:32.947 --> 00:12:34.835
It really smells like egg.

00:12:34.835 --> 00:12:36.979
Presentation wise, I think this looks

00:12:36.979 --> 00:12:38.813
like it could be bread.

00:12:38.813 --> 00:12:40.262
Yeah, I think without the egg wash,

00:12:40.262 --> 00:12:42.664
it would look just like

00:12:42.664 --> 00:12:44.171
a really nice attempt at bread.

00:12:44.171 --> 00:12:45.441
- [Keith] Yeah, I think I fucked it up

00:12:45.441 --> 00:12:47.193
right at the end there.

00:12:47.193 --> 00:12:48.443
Give it a shot.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:50.513
Oh my god.

00:12:50.513 --> 00:12:51.346
- [Keith] Give it a chance.

00:12:51.346 --> 00:12:52.179
What do you think?

00:12:52.179 --> 00:12:53.012
Oh my god.

00:12:53.012 --> 00:12:55.131
- [Zack] It's got zero flavor.

00:12:55.131 --> 00:12:56.058
Well, it's got to have some flavor,

00:12:56.058 --> 00:12:57.435
you're really reacting.

00:12:57.435 --> 00:12:58.893
And it's underbaked.

00:12:58.893 --> 00:12:59.726
Oh, fuck.

00:12:59.726 --> 00:13:01.052
Let's see if it bounces.

00:13:01.052 --> 00:13:03.106
(laughter)

00:13:03.106 --> 00:13:05.276
You'd think that it would have less--

00:13:05.276 --> 00:13:06.693
Mmm. It's good.

00:13:08.308 --> 00:13:10.990
So, judges, is it bread?

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:11.838
Yes.

00:13:11.838 --> 00:13:13.150
This is definitely bread.

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:13.983
We can give it that.

00:13:13.983 --> 00:13:15.166
We can give it that.

00:13:15.166 --> 00:13:18.353
(applause and cheers)

00:13:18.353 --> 00:13:19.370
- [Eugene] Alright, judges.

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:20.214
- [Hannah] Wow.

00:13:20.214 --> 00:13:22.189
- [Alexis] Oh, it's beautiful.

00:13:22.189 --> 00:13:24.212
It's beautiful!

00:13:24.212 --> 00:13:26.778
This is Eugene's Drunken Spice Loaf.

00:13:26.778 --> 00:13:28.011
Were you drunk when you made it?

00:13:28.011 --> 00:13:29.118
I was.

00:13:29.118 --> 00:13:30.151
The color is good.

00:13:30.151 --> 00:13:30.984
The color's better.

00:13:30.984 --> 00:13:32.665
The braid is beautifully done.

00:13:32.665 --> 00:13:33.498
- [Hannah] Ready?

00:13:33.498 --> 00:13:34.975
And rip.

00:13:34.975 --> 00:13:36.712
Oooh!
Oooh!

00:13:36.712 --> 00:13:37.954
Wow.

00:13:37.954 --> 00:13:39.260
Look at this!

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:40.098
It looks really good.

00:13:40.098 --> 00:13:43.137
- [Hannah] This feels like bread.

00:13:43.137 --> 00:13:43.970
Oh.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.481
- [Hannah] Oh wow.

00:13:45.481 --> 00:13:47.478
That is great.

00:13:47.478 --> 00:13:49.998
I would almost swallow this.

00:13:49.998 --> 00:13:51.025
I will.

00:13:51.025 --> 00:13:51.859
- [Eugene] I'll take it.
Really?

00:13:51.859 --> 00:13:52.692
Yes, this is--

00:13:52.692 --> 00:13:53.875
My slice is good!

00:13:53.875 --> 00:13:57.096
I just feel like it's old beer.

00:13:57.096 --> 00:13:58.951
It is three bottles of beer.

00:13:58.951 --> 00:13:59.861
You might have gotten

00:13:59.861 --> 00:14:01.507
a lot of star anise in your slice.

00:14:01.507 --> 00:14:03.299
I didn't know how it was proportioned.

00:14:03.299 --> 00:14:04.999
Is this your first time making bread?

00:14:04.999 --> 00:14:06.899
Yeah, it's my first time.

00:14:06.899 --> 00:14:07.754
Not a bad job at all.

00:14:07.754 --> 00:14:08.942
No, no.

00:14:08.942 --> 00:14:11.335
Actually slightly impressive.

00:14:11.335 --> 00:14:13.485
(booing)

00:14:13.485 --> 00:14:14.774
Boo, he was a mess!

00:14:14.774 --> 00:14:16.630
So the final question is,

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:17.995
is it bread?

00:14:17.995 --> 00:14:19.039
Absolutely.

00:14:19.039 --> 00:14:19.872
Am I still drunk?

00:14:19.872 --> 00:14:22.260
Because I wasn't expecting these answers.

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.093
Okay, Zach.

00:14:23.093 --> 00:14:24.702
Please present your bread.

00:14:24.702 --> 00:14:25.982
Judges, today we've seen

00:14:25.982 --> 00:14:27.304
where bread has been.

00:14:27.304 --> 00:14:28.331
I'm going to show you

00:14:28.331 --> 00:14:30.121
where bread is going, if you will.

00:14:30.121 --> 00:14:31.149
An introduction.

00:14:31.149 --> 00:14:34.307
- [Zach] I present my take
on the buckwheat bread:

00:14:34.307 --> 00:14:35.974
The Bucksweet Bread.

00:14:36.816 --> 00:14:38.375
What forest floor did you

00:14:38.375 --> 00:14:40.220
pick this up off of?

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:41.239
You're telling me that if you

00:14:41.239 --> 00:14:43.143
walked into an organic food restaurant,

00:14:43.143 --> 00:14:44.098
and you saw that, you wouldn't be like,

00:14:44.098 --> 00:14:45.150
"Yeah, I'm intrigued."?

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.510
You know, it look rustic.

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.157
- [Zach] Thank you, thank you.

00:14:48.157 --> 00:14:50.306
I don't want to eat it.

00:14:50.306 --> 00:14:51.394
Cause you just want to lick at it all day.

00:14:51.394 --> 00:14:52.227
Because it's so beautiful.

00:14:52.227 --> 00:14:53.060
I get it.

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:55.346
- [Hannah] I'm just going to...

00:14:55.346 --> 00:14:56.554
Does it look like bread?

00:14:56.554 --> 00:14:57.814
No.
No.

00:14:57.814 --> 00:14:59.604
Are there sprinkles in here?

00:14:59.604 --> 00:15:01.989
- [Hannah] Oh, I like that it just falls.

00:15:01.989 --> 00:15:04.786
- [Zach] It's a crumble
loaf, did I not mention that?

00:15:04.786 --> 00:15:06.355
I'm real confident with this one.

00:15:06.355 --> 00:15:07.188
I can't-- It's funny.

00:15:07.188 --> 00:15:09.199
I can't actually seem to pick it up.

00:15:09.199 --> 00:15:10.032
- [Zach] Come on, Zack.

00:15:10.032 --> 00:15:11.314
From one Zach to another.

00:15:11.314 --> 00:15:13.169
No. Nonono.

00:15:13.169 --> 00:15:14.338
Just put your tongue on it.

00:15:14.338 --> 00:15:15.228
We lost Zack, that's fine.

00:15:15.228 --> 00:15:16.598
There's only room for one Zach in here.

00:15:16.598 --> 00:15:17.431
Got my girls.

00:15:17.431 --> 00:15:18.431
Oh, come on.

00:15:20.189 --> 00:15:22.385
That is the worst food

00:15:22.385 --> 00:15:23.952
I've ever tried in my life.

00:15:23.952 --> 00:15:25.663
Wow.
Wow, you did it.

00:15:25.663 --> 00:15:27.552
I didn't know I'd be
getting a superlative today.

00:15:27.552 --> 00:15:28.622
That's amazing.

00:15:28.622 --> 00:15:30.728
It's truly terrible.

00:15:30.728 --> 00:15:33.294
I actually am covered in chills.

00:15:33.294 --> 00:15:35.544
I swallowed at least ten percent of that.

00:15:35.544 --> 00:15:36.983
That's not the goal.

00:15:36.983 --> 00:15:38.530
You could not pay me to eat this.

00:15:38.530 --> 00:15:39.697
Is it bread?

00:15:40.666 --> 00:15:42.924
This is not bread, at all.

00:15:42.924 --> 00:15:45.211
Right, because it's next level.

00:15:45.211 --> 00:15:46.803
Uh, no, this is not bread.

00:15:46.803 --> 00:15:47.947
Chefs, thank you.

00:15:47.947 --> 00:15:48.780
You know, I can leave this

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:50.298
wherever you want.

00:15:50.298 --> 00:15:51.592
No, you should burn it.

00:15:51.592 --> 00:15:52.853
So, judges.

00:15:52.853 --> 00:15:54.748
What do you think?

00:15:54.748 --> 00:15:56.936
On the bright side, we
know which is the worst.

00:15:56.936 --> 00:15:58.043
- [Zack] Oh, yeah.

00:15:58.043 --> 00:15:59.492
Ned's was really beautiful.

00:15:59.492 --> 00:16:00.400
True.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.083
If he had been going for bundt cake,

00:16:03.083 --> 00:16:04.396
he would have really nailed it.

00:16:04.396 --> 00:16:05.502
And if he had used sugar.

00:16:05.502 --> 00:16:06.940
- [Hannah] Keith's.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:07.806
- [Zack] It looked like a

00:16:07.806 --> 00:16:09.582
big pterodactyl egg to me.

00:16:09.582 --> 00:16:11.576
Keith's I liked a little,

00:16:11.576 --> 00:16:12.908
because I like eggs.

00:16:12.908 --> 00:16:13.799
Eugene's?

00:16:13.799 --> 00:16:15.212
- [Zack] What was very impressive, that--

00:16:15.212 --> 00:16:16.045
- [Alexis] That braid?

00:16:16.045 --> 00:16:16.878
- [Zack] Yeah, that braided it up.

00:16:16.878 --> 00:16:18.940
The piece you had was more edible.

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:20.548
I was thinking about swallowing it.

00:16:20.548 --> 00:16:22.314
Joan, I believe we're in agreement.

00:16:22.314 --> 00:16:25.184
Okay, let's call them back in.

00:16:25.184 --> 00:16:28.951
(sweet piano music)

00:16:28.951 --> 00:16:30.640
(kid baas)

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.305
So, welcome back, bakers.

00:16:32.305 --> 00:16:35.555
The judges have given us their results.

00:16:36.635 --> 00:16:37.597
Are you ready?

00:16:37.597 --> 00:16:38.430
Fourth...

00:16:40.242 --> 00:16:41.138
...is Zach.

00:16:41.138 --> 00:16:42.892
The challenge was to make bread,

00:16:42.892 --> 00:16:44.225
and you did not.

00:16:45.062 --> 00:16:46.729
And third, we have

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:48.673
Ned.

00:16:51.244 --> 00:16:52.216
It looked nice when it came out.

00:16:52.216 --> 00:16:53.321
It looked really nice, Ned.

00:16:53.321 --> 00:16:54.154
- [Hannah] Really good job.

00:16:54.154 --> 00:16:55.653
- [Alexis] Really nice.

00:16:55.653 --> 00:16:57.236
So on the second,

00:16:59.066 --> 00:17:00.233
we have Keith.

00:17:01.467 --> 00:17:02.583
- [Zack] The dinosaur egg.

00:17:02.583 --> 00:17:03.416
You really have a future

00:17:03.416 --> 00:17:05.608
in almost sort of making bread.

00:17:05.608 --> 00:17:06.960
- [Joan] And now for the big finale.

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:09.084
Wonder who it could be?

00:17:09.084 --> 00:17:11.932
I'm pleased to announce...

00:17:11.932 --> 00:17:13.485
Eugene.
Eugene.

00:17:13.485 --> 00:17:14.960
Congratulations!

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:16.257
Yay, thank you!

00:17:16.257 --> 00:17:18.597
I've been asking for hugs all day.

00:17:18.597 --> 00:17:20.368
I really think it was the coloring

00:17:20.368 --> 00:17:21.513
and the distribution that--

00:17:21.513 --> 00:17:23.736
That's what edged everybody out, you know?

00:17:23.736 --> 00:17:25.094
You actually had something

00:17:25.094 --> 00:17:27.192
that was kind of like a crust.

00:17:27.192 --> 00:17:28.279
It's not good.

00:17:28.279 --> 00:17:30.960
- [Zack] No no no. Let's
not get confused here.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:32.251
It's not good.

00:17:32.251 --> 00:17:34.159
It is the best out of the others.

00:17:34.159 --> 00:17:35.733
(judges laugh)

00:17:35.733 --> 00:17:36.938
I think we learned how to

00:17:36.938 --> 00:17:38.335
accidentally make bread.

00:17:38.335 --> 00:17:39.753
This inspired me to try cooking

00:17:39.753 --> 00:17:41.359
more than I do now.

00:17:41.359 --> 00:17:42.789
Can't help but say I'm
incredibly discouraged

00:17:42.789 --> 00:17:44.640
about the outcome of today's video.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:46.245
I tried so hard to engineer a video

00:17:46.245 --> 00:17:48.559
that couldn't end the
same way all videos end.

00:17:48.559 --> 00:17:49.718
Sometimes you take risks.

00:17:49.718 --> 00:17:51.408
And like Eugene, it pays off.

00:17:51.408 --> 00:17:54.370
Other times, those risks do not pay off.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:55.389
I want to try and bake bread

00:17:55.389 --> 00:17:56.712
with a recipe next time.

00:17:56.712 --> 00:17:58.258
I feel like I could
have really nailed this

00:17:58.258 --> 00:18:01.454
if I just had a couple
of simple instructions.

00:18:01.454 --> 00:18:03.352
Eugene's did taste better, okay!?

00:18:03.352 --> 00:18:04.185
I'll admit it!

00:18:04.185 --> 00:18:05.315
That's what I'm upset about.

00:18:05.315 --> 00:18:06.648
His bread was better!

00:18:06.648 --> 00:18:08.268
I'm not mad because I think

00:18:08.268 --> 00:18:10.096
that his wasn't better
and I should have won.

00:18:10.096 --> 00:18:11.444
He should have won.

00:18:11.444 --> 00:18:13.441
I'm mad that I wanted to win more

00:18:13.441 --> 00:18:15.169
and I didn't!

00:18:15.169 --> 00:18:17.329
I'm disappointed in myself!

00:18:17.329 --> 00:18:19.408
And I've been externalizing all my anger

00:18:19.408 --> 00:18:21.145
on Eugene and other people but

00:18:21.145 --> 00:18:23.637
I'm mad at my own shortcomings.

00:18:23.637 --> 00:18:26.229
Shouldn't have put the egg on top!

00:18:26.229 --> 00:18:29.312
(offscreen laughter)

00:18:31.212 --> 00:18:32.303
(kid quietly baas)

